    "limitations": [
      "One run per model/task; source repeat check found about one score point and 2.4x cost variation. Sub-one-point ordering is not robust evidence.",
      "Cross-batch CLI versions and dates drift; environmental comparability is not established.",
      "Manual quality review contributes 7 to 12 points per task according to the source.",
      "Re-review increased historical GPT-5.6 Luna and GPT-6 Luna C3 scores by 0.31 and 0.30. Earlier snapshot figures are not silently updated.",
      "DeepSeek-V4-Flash is reported as BYOK, so transport/auth/accounting differs from hosted CLI entries.",
      "The article says a chart script can reproduce plots; earlier repository-tree research did not find that complete runner/aggregator/script at its fixed commit. This migration does not claim that upstream reproduction was verified.",
      "References to twelve/fifteen-configuration intermediate reports are historical timeline mentions, not additional Library pages read or migrated."
    ]
